  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"./assets/hero.png\" width=\"100%\" alt=\"dsh-call-session hero\" />\n</p>\n\n<h1 align=\"center\">dsh-call-session</h1>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  Run several DeepSeek Harness sessions side by side, hand work from one to another, and watch the whole collaboration on one read-only canvas.\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/popu2do/dsh-call-session/blob/master/LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg\" alt=\"License: MIT\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"./docs/adrs/README.md\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/ADR-Standard-green.svg\" alt=\"ADR Architecture\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://nodejs.org\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Node.js-%3E%3D20.0.0-339933.svg?logo=node.js&logoColor=white\" alt=\"Node.js Version\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://cordis.moe\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Cordis-v4.x-purple.svg\" alt=\"Cordis\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://www.typescriptlang.org/\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-Strict-3178C6.svg?logo=typescript&logoColor=white\" alt=\"TypeScript Strict\" /></a>\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  English | <a href=\"README_ZH.md\">简体中文</a>\n</p>\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Canvas",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"./assets/canvas-demo.png\" width=\"100%\" alt=\"dsh-call-session canvas\" />\n</p>\n\nTwo long-running sessions hand work to each other; the canvas shows both workspaces, the session nodes, the shared blackboard items and the call traces between them."
    },
    {
      "section": "Canvas",
      "text": "- Topology: workspace columns, running/idle session nodes, blackboard items with TTL countdowns, and directional call traces.\n- Interaction: hovering highlights the 1-hop connected subgraph; double-clicking opens a read-only inspector drawer.\n- Read-only boundary: the canvas offers no control inputs; all state changes originate from the agents themselves.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Mention",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"./assets/mention-demo.png\" width=\"100%\" alt=\"dsh-call-session mention\" />\n</p>\n\nType `@` in the composer to reference another session: the title is inserted into the message as a reference chip, and the model receives that session's read-only content."
    },
    {
      "section": "Mention",
      "text": "- Pick a workspace, then a session: the workspace list marks the current workspace first and keeps the rest in sidebar order, the drilled workspace lists its sessions most recently active first with nothing pinned, and subagent or archived sessions never show.\n- The referenced session is not woken, no call is dispatched, and no connection appears on the canvas.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Overview",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness sessions are isolated by default, and child tasks exit upon completion."
    },
    {
      "section": "Overview",
      "text": "`dsh-call-session` adds in-process cross-session communication, peer session creation, and shared blackboard capabilities:\n- Inter-session unicast: send directives or hand off tasks between independent long-running sessions.\n- Shared blackboard: publish bulky artifacts to a shared board for on-demand retrieval, avoiding context bloat.\n- Visual canvas: observe session states, blackboard items, and call trajectories in the DSH Web UI.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Add to target profile web",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-call-session"
    },
    {
      "section": "List installed plugins",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web list"
    },
    {
      "section": "Remove plugin",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-call-session\n```\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Scenarios",
      "text": "Instruct the agent using plain natural language in the chat; the agent invokes the tools automatically:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Task Handoff",
      "text": "User prompt:\n> Hand off this task summary to the \"audit-session\" session.\n\nThe agent calls `session_call` to dispatch a unicast message. If the target session is running, it steers execution; if idle, it wakes a new turn."
    },
    {
      "section": "Post Results",
      "text": "User prompt:\n> Publish the review conclusions to the board and notify relevant sessions to pick up tasks.\n\nThe agent calls `board_post` to store the detailed report on the blackboard and obtain a `postId`. Other sessions retrieve the content on demand via `board_list`, preventing context window explosion."
    },
    {
      "section": "Create Session",
      "text": "User prompt:\n> Create a new session and hand off tasks.\n\nThe agent calls `session_create` to spawn a long-running peer session in the current workspace, automatically inheriting model specifications and presets."
    },
    {
      "section": "Reference Session",
      "text": "User prompt:\n> @ Architecture Review Agent, re-check the revised contract against it.\n\nNaming the session in plain words reaches the same place:\n> Ask the Architecture Review Agent to re-check the revised contract against it.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Type | Mode | Common Use Case |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `session_call` | Tool | Push | 1:1 unicast call for task dispatch, progress reporting, and handoffs |\n| `session_create` | Tool | Native | Create long-running peer sessions for parallel multi-role collaboration |\n| `session_query` | Tool | Read-only | List sessions and check active/idle statuses in or across workspaces |\n| `board_post` | Tool | Pull | Publish blackboard entries for large artifacts and shared milestones |\n| `board_list` | Tool | Pull | Query blackboard records by ID, topic, or digest mode |\n| `board_clear` | Tool | Manage | Dismiss or purge completed and expired blackboard entries |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Comparison",
      "text": "| Mechanism | Type | Model | When to Use |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `subagent` | Built-in | Hierarchical delegation, ephemeral child task, exits on completion | Scoped exploration, code search, one-off script execution. |\n| `dsh-call-session` | Plugin | Peer-to-peer collaboration, in-process unicast messaging and shared board | Directives and status sync between independent top-level sessions, or sharing large outputs. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Comparison",
      "text": "Selection guidelines:\n- Prefer built-in: for isolated, scoped tasks, use DSH built-in `subagent` directly.\n- Use on demand: when multiple independent top-level sessions need to coordinate or share large context via a blackboard, use `dsh-call-session`.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Config",
      "text": "The plugin runs with built-in defaults out of the box.\n\nTo customize, add property overrides to `~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n- id: dsh-call-session\n  config:\n    debounceMs: 500\n    maxCapacity: 500"
    },
    {
      "section": "Config",
      "text": "Options:\n- `enabled`: boolean, default `true`. Enable or disable plugin tools.\n- `debounceMs`: number, default `300`. Atomic disk write debounce delay in milliseconds.\n- `maxCapacity`: number, default `200`. Maximum board entries.\n- `telemetryCapacity`: number, default `200`. Maximum call traces retained in canvas data buffer.\n- `locale`: string, default `'auto'`. Interaction language preference (`'auto'`, `'zh'`, `'en'`).\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "Technical decisions are recorded as Architecture Decision Records (ADRs):\n\n- Decision catalog: see [docs/adrs/README.md](./docs/adrs/README.md).\n- Architecture topology: see [docs/architecture/](./docs/architecture/).\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "| Environment | Supported | Verified |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| DeepSeek Harness | `>=0.2.0-rc.2 <0.3.0-0` | `0.2.0-rc.2`, `0.2.1-rc.2`, `0.2.1-rc.5`, `0.2.2-rc.1` |\n| Cordis | `^4.0.2` | `4.0.2+` |\n| Node.js | `>=20.0.0` | `20.x`, `22.x` |\n\n---"
    },
